course: dictionary
lesson: 3365
title: Exclude and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word exclude means to keep someone or something out, or to leave it out on purpose. To work out which meaning is used, read the context. Ask yourself: is something being kept out, left out of a count, or sent away?
explain: «Connor was excluded (sent home from school) for two days.» The brackets give you the clue: excluded means sent away from school as a punishment. In maths the context is different: «Count from 1 to 10 excluding 5» means count the numbers but leave 5 out.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Count from 1 to 10 excluding 5» still makes sense with leave out 5 in place of excluding. Feelings matter too: if you feel excluded from a game, you feel left out, and that hurts. Be kind and include others.
fact: Exclude means to keep out, to leave out on purpose, to send away from school as a punishment, or to decide that something is not possible.
fact: «Excluding» means leaving something out of a total, as in «the price excluding tax».
fact: «Connor was excluded (sent home from school) for two days.» Here excluded means sent away from school for a time.
fact: Exclude is the opposite of include, which means to take something in or let it join.
fact: Useful phrases: «exclude from», «excluding VAT», and «feel excluded».
exercise: «Count from 1 to 10 excluding 5.» What does excluding mean here? | *Leaving 5 out of the count | Taking away every number | Adding 5 to the total | Counting 5 twice
exercise: «Connor was excluded (sent home from school) for two days.» What does excluded mean in this sentence? | Invited to a party | Given a prize for good work | Kept in for lunch | *Sent away from school as a punishment
exercise: Maya says, "I feel excluded when I'm not picked for the game." What does excluded mean for Maya? | Too tired to play | Sent to the head teacher | *Left out and not taking part | Happy and busy with her friends
test: Which phrase means the price without tax? | *the price excluding VAT | the price including VAT | the price for VAT only
test: Which word is the opposite of exclude? | argue | forget | *include
exam: «It is impossible for the sun to rise at midnight, so we can exclude that idea.» What does exclude mean in this sentence? | Send it away from school | Count it in the total | *Decide that it is not possible | Keep it safe in a box
